Package: reproducibility
Title: Audit the Reproducibility of Research Projects and Articles
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Pablo", "Sánchez-Núñez", email = "psancheznunez@outlook.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"), comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-7845-9506"))
Description: Audits the conditions for reproducing research. For a
    project directory, checks documentation, licence, citation metadata,
    declared and pinned dependencies, containers, pipelines, continuous
    integration, data availability and documentation, absolute paths,
    random seeds and large files, each with its evidence and the guideline
    it comes from, such as the FAIR principles for research software
    (Barker et al., 2022, <doi:10.1038/s41597-022-01710-x>). For an article,
    detects data and code availability, availability statements,
    preregistration and shared materials in the full text with explicit,
    versioned rules; a text that cannot be read is unverifiable, never
    "no". Writes HTML and JSON reports, creates reproducible project
    skeletons and a 'GitHub Actions' workflow that runs the audit.
